<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Magnitude of a vector and a distance</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Give exact values or decimals to 2 decimal places.</p><p>(a) Find the magnitude of \({@matrix([vv[1]],[vv[2]])@}\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) On a map with 1 unit = 1 km, a school S is at \(({@A[1]@},\,{@A[2]@})\) and a clinic K at \(({@B[1]@},\,{@B[2]@})\). How far is the clinic from the school in a straight line?</p><div>[[input:ans2]] km [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Pythagoras on the across and up moves: \(|\mathbf{v}| = \sqrt{x^2 + y^2}\).</p><p>(a) \(\sqrt{({@vv[1]@})^2 + ({@vv[2]@})^2} = \sqrt{{@S@}}\) [[if test="integerp(tm1)"]]\(= {@tm1@}\).[[else]]\(\approx {@m1d@}\).[[/if]]</p><p>(b) \(\overrightarrow{SK}\) is end minus start: \({@matrix([d[1]],[d[2]])@}\). Its magnitude is \(\sqrt{({@d[1]@})^2 + ({@d[2]@})^2} = \sqrt{{@Sd@}}\) [[if test="integerp(tm2)"]]\(= {@tm2@}\)[[else]]\(\approx {@m2d@}\)[[/if]] km.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: magnitude of a vector and the distance between two points by Pythagoras, map context. Entries 1 to 5 have whole magnitudes, 6 to 10 surds; every v has one negative component; diagnostics are more than 2 x 0.00501 apart and from the generic offset. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Section B, B5(b). */
mlist: [[[15,-8],[1,-4],[-3,0]],[[-24,7],[-6,6],[-2,2]],[[12,-5],[-1,-3],[-4,0]],[[-40,9],[-3,5],[6,-1]],[[12,-9],[-3,2],[4,-4]],[[8,-3],[4,-2],[-5,0]],[[-2,9],[0,3],[7,1]],[[5,-8],[-2,6],[4,0]],[[6,-5],[6,2],[-5,3]],[[-3,10],[5,-3],[-3,1]]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
vv: mlist[ix][1]; A: mlist[ix][2]; B: mlist[ix][3];
S: vv[1]^2+vv[2]^2; tm1: sqrt(S);
d: B-A; Sd: d[1]^2+d[2]^2; tm2: sqrt(Sd);
neg: if vv[1]<0 then vv[1] else vv[2];
/* diagnostics (a): no root, sum of sizes, sum of components, negative squared as negative */
e1: abs(vv[1])+abs(vv[2]); e2: abs(vv[1]+vv[2]); e3: sqrt(abs(vv[1]^2-vv[2]^2));
/* diagnostics (b): no root, added the coordinates, |OK|, sum of sizes */
f1: sqrt((A[1]+B[1])^2+(A[2]+B[2])^2); f2: sqrt(B[1]^2+B[2]^2); f3: abs(d[1])+abs(d[2]);
r1: float(floor(100*tm1+1/2)/100); r2: float(floor(100*tm2+1/2)/100);
m1d: dispdp(r1,2); m2d: dispdp(r2,2);
w1: float(tm1)+0.5; w2: float(tm2)+0.5;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, |v|={@m1d@}, SK={@m2d@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors: magnitude of a vector and a distance</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 2.2: Find the magnitude of a column vector and the straight-line distance between two places on a map, exactly or to 2 decimal places.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question B5(b) in Section B of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: new numbers, Kenyan context, STACK randomisation, the magnitude of a column added, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
